#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110293 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d203cc5-4e76-5f78-b431-b357164de3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Right Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "afde7d46-5a88-5ec8-b86f-32d126a36258" :question/math-academy-id "e-10595" :question/problem "Which of the following shows a right angle?\n\n![](images/e6/e6ee9f2a0b7dfa70c1d61dac0d19e1347d56ba94d93762c435d0727216d61143.png)" :question/worked-solution "An angle of $90^\\circ$ has the same measure as one-quarter of a full turn.\n\nAmong the given options, the only $90^\\circ$ angle is the following:\n\n![](images/b2/b2e63cd5919753a0b549f345ecfa5dbfa40bf5d85a3dbe8b59872119316d1dd7.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110294 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110673 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5701fed-0320-54da-8983-71c572ab1e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Straight Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "5427c83b-5f34-57fa-b56c-a0c190e74348" :question/math-academy-id "e-10596" :question/problem "Which of the following shows a straight angle?\n\n![](images/e6/e6ee9f2a0b7dfa70c1d61dac0d19e1347d56ba94d93762c435d0727216d61143.png)" :question/worked-solution "A straight angle has a degree measure of $180^\\circ.$ This corresponds to one-half of a full turn.\n\nAmong the given options, the only straight angle is the following:\n\n \n\n![](images/1e/1e16add703d800bce68d70ded10f220808accb557ae15f9245147eaf3ca513b1.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b4df4d5-4ffc-53f0-8207-f710351f7456" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Null and Full Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "154c65b2-4d51-5da0-b00c-293f3fba3bd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-2604" :question/problem "![](images/86/867b3664e93f42c55a2f97dc28bf66794484e226981632c85f725926cec77def.png)\n\nWhat type of angle is $\\angle RST,$ shown in the figure above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the vertex of $\\angle RST$ is point $S,$ not point $T.$ So $\\angle RST$ is *not* a straight angle.\n\nAs a result, the two rays $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{SR}$ and $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{ST}$ of our angle coincide. So, we can think of $\\angle RST$ as:\n\n- A *null* angle, assuming it doesn't turn at all.\n\n![](images/a8/a8916a724d4463bf2047c919b73770160d3124838b61af0dcdc2b9e04322381a.png)\n\n- A *full* angle, assuming it makes one full turn.\n\n![](images/9c/9cd768b4361e95a18ffa52d6315fb5ea6cd0cf6784bc4c9e12b1bae1f6566755.png)\n\nSo, the answer is \"Null\" or \"Full.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b4df4d5-4ffc-53f0-8207-f710351f7456" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Null and Full Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d0a706-cb3a-5b0e-9560-36044c90c85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Null or Full" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431204} {:answer/id #uuid "9a066ffd-6ea2-566d-a2b2-e694aaac02f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Straight" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431229} {:answer/id #uuid "d03c3a92-f7e4-5e74-a82b-0e955bcccd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Right" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431242} {:answer/id #uuid "d53144d2-e238-57e8-85d5-4a0cdbc1fab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Full or Straight" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431243} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6d9f18-1923-502a-8288-ff8f30c229c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24d0a706-cb3a-5b0e-9560-36044c90c85d" :answ